Package: journalcheck
Architecture: all
Depends: ${python3:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, python3-systemd, python3-yaml
Enhances: system-log-daemon, systemd
Description: Systemd journal monitoring and notification tool
 A tool for auditing systemd journal entries with configurable priority
 filtering, pattern matching, and security violation detection.
 .
 Key features:
  * Priority-based filtering (emerg, alert, crit, err, warning, notice, info, debug)
  * Per-service priority configuration
  * Regex pattern matching for violations and ignore rules
  * Pre-configured security patterns for common services (sshd, sudo, su, smartd)
  * Cursor-based tracking (only process new entries)
  * Multiple output formats (short, json)
  * Flexible notification via email, commands, or stdout
  * Systemd timer integration for automated monitoring
 .
 Inspired by logcheck but designed for systemd's journal with modern features
 like JSON output and flexible notification options.
